1. HTML (index.html)

The HTML file provides the structure of the website.

Header: Contains the logo and navigation links (Home, About, Projects, Contact)

Hero Section: Introduction with name and tagline, with a "Contact Me" button

About Section: Brief description with a "Read More" toggle

Projects Section: Displays 3 sample projects with titles and descriptions

Contact Section: Form with Name, Email, and Message fields

Footer: Contains copyright information

Semantic elements used: <header>, <nav>, <section>, <footer>, <h1>, <h2>, <p>, <button>, <form>

2. CSS (styles.css)

The CSS file defines the look and feel of the website.

Body styling: Font, color, background, smooth scrolling

Header & Navigation: Background color, sticky position, hover effects

Sections: Padding, border-radius, shadows, responsive layout

Project Cards: Hover animations, box shadows, color changes

Contact Form: Input focus effects, submit button styling

Dark/Light Mode: Toggle between dark and light theme

Responsive Design: Media queries for mobile screens

3. JavaScript (script.js)

Hamburger Menu: Toggles navigation links on smaller screens

Smooth Scroll: Smoothly scrolls to sections when navigation links or buttons are clicked

About Section Toggle: Shows or hides the "Read More" text

Contact Form: Displays success or error message on submission

Dark/Light Mode Toggle: Switches between dark and light theme and updates button text

4. Features Implemented

Responsive layout for desktop and mobile devices

Dark/Light mode toggle

Smooth scrolling navigation

Interactive "Read More" toggle in About section

Hover animations on project cards and buttons

Contact form UI (frontend only, no backend submission)

Summary:
This personal portfolio website demonstrates the use of HTML5 for structure, CSS3 for styling and responsive design, and JavaScript for interactivity. All assignment requirements have been implemented, providing a clean, modern, and responsive user interface.
